{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2695 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "a2139cfe59aac5945483c760c6c01cf5240815a6ef49be0f7465c1ec0a52d137" :edb/db-before-t 2694 :edb/db-after-t 2695 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536007 50 #inst "2026-10-09T12:47:54.383Z" 13194139536007 true] [17592186229140 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379200 13194139536007 true] [17592186229140 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379204 13194139536007 true] [17592186229140 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379207 13194139536007 true] [17592186379200 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379201 13194139536007 true] [17592186379200 1089 "q-350548" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379200 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536007 true] [17592186379200 1100 "Given that $I(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4x+{t}^{5})^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,$ calculate ${I}^{′}(t)$ for $t\\in R$ by differentiating under the integral sign.\n\n${I}^{′}(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379200 1113 #uuid "11d0068f-c50c-56c9-ac9d-c760f1b21cef" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379200 1145 "Suppose $f(x,t)$ is continuous on $R=[a,b]\\times [c,d]$ and $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}$ exists and is continuous on $R.$ Then, the function\n\n$$\nF(t)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nis differentiable on $(c,d),$ and\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\frac{∂f}{∂t}(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis is known as *differentiating under the integral sign.*\n\nWe wish to compute ${I}^{′}(t),$ where\n\n$$\nI(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4x+{t}^{5})^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating under the integral sign, we get\n\n$$\n{I}^{′}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(4x+{t}^{5})^{2}]\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, let's compute the partial derivative with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(4x+{t}^{5})^{2}] & =2(4x+{t}^{5})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂t}(4x+{t}^{5}) \\\\  & =2(4x+{t}^{5})\\cdot 5{t}^{4} \\\\  & =10{t}^{4}(4x+{t}^{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this back into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}^{′}(t) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10{t}^{4}(4x+{t}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10{t}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4x+{t}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's evaluate the remaining integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4x+{t}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{1}+{t}^{5}x{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2+{t}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{I}^{′}(t)=10{t}^{4}(2+{t}^{5}).\n$$" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379201 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379202 13194139536007 true] [17592186379201 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379203 13194139536007 true] [17592186379201 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536007 true] [17592186379201 1041 "field-1" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379201 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379202 13194139536007 true] [17592186379201 1110 #uuid "b01e1ddf-a21a-5597-a6fc-26a62b71e64a" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379202 1034 "20t^4+10t^9" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379202 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536007 true] [17592186379202 1111 #uuid "65338c66-e928-50a3-9616-fbfda716827b" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379203 1034 "20t^4+10t^5" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379203 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536007 true] [17592186379203 1111 #uuid "5bd545d1-de75-59e3-a4de-b5e07bb5d71b" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379204 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379205 13194139536007 true] [17592186379204 1089 "q-350550" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379204 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536007 true] [17592186379204 1100 "Given that $I(t)={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}+{t}^{4})^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,$ calculate ${I}^{′}(t)$ for $t\\in R$ by differentiating under the integral sign.\n\n${I}^{′}(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379204 1113 #uuid "47e13c43-3d7e-5887-8a06-229459d7d60b" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379204 1145 "Suppose $f(x,t)$ is continuous on $R=[a,b]\\times [c,d]$ and $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}$ exists and is continuous on $R.$ Then, the function\n\n$$\nF(t)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nis differentiable on $(c,d),$ and\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\frac{∂f}{∂t}(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis is known as *differentiating under the integral sign.*\n\nWe wish to compute ${I}^{′}(t),$ where\n\n$$\nI(t)={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}+{t}^{4})^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating under the integral sign, we get\n\n$$\n{I}^{′}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[({x}^{2}+{t}^{4})^{2}]\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, let's compute the partial derivative with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[({x}^{2}+{t}^{4})^{2}] & =2({x}^{2}+{t}^{4})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂t}({x}^{2}+{t}^{4}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}+{t}^{4})\\cdot 4{t}^{3} \\\\  & =8{t}^{3}({x}^{2}+{t}^{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this back into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}^{′}(t) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}8{t}^{3}({x}^{2}+{t}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{t}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}+{t}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's evaluate the remaining integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}+{t}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{0}^{2}+{t}^{4}x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}+2{t}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{I}^{′}(t)=8{t}^{3}(\\frac{8}{3}+2{t}^{4}).\n$$" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379206 13194139536007 true] [17592186379205 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536007 true] [17592186379205 1041 "field-1" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379205 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379206 13194139536007 true] [17592186379205 1110 #uuid "d0686e5e-b3bc-5db8-a7fd-a2659198ecb5" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379206 1034 "\\frac{64}{3}t^3+16t^7" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379206 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536007 true] [17592186379206 1111 #uuid "69a0b7ad-9c2f-5f95-bde4-a3524ee2abb9" 13194139536007 true] [17592186379207 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379208 131941395360